  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«tu» imperative",
     "texto": [
      "With **tu**, the imperative is almost the same as the «ele» form: **Fala** (speak), **come** (eat), **vem** (come), **diz** (say), **dá** (give).",
      "Exception: **ser** → **sê** (be). **Estar** → **está** (stay / be)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pronouns after the verb",
     "texto": [
      "With the affirmative imperative, the pronoun goes **after** the verb, with a hyphen: **Diz-me** (tell me), **Dá-me** (give me), **Diz-lhe** (tell him / her), **Vai-te** (go away).",
      "Watch out: **Faz-lo** does not exist: it is written **fá-lo** (do it) because the verb lost the -z."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
